  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 518.04 Appointment",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 518.04 Appointment.\n\n(a) The director shall review each application submitted pursuant to Saf-C 518.02 and the results of any interview conducted pursuant to Saf-C 518.03. Following the review, the director shall determine whether to appoint an applicant as a municipal agent.\n\n(b) No appointment shall be effective without the approval of the commissioner.\n\n(c) No appointment shall be effective, regardless of any effective date noted in any certificate of appointment, until the appointee:\n\n(1) Signs the contract required by Saf-C 518.05;\n\n(2) Completes the training requirements set forth in Saf-C 518.06; and\n\n(3) Files the bond required by Saf-C 518.08.\n\n(d) Each appointment shall be conditioned upon the appointee's adherence to all aspects of the contract required by Saf-C 518.05, as well as all the requirements set forth in these rules pertaining to the duties and responsibilities of a municipal agent. Any appointment shall be revoked pursuant to RSA 261:74-f, II, for failure to adhere to the contract or failure to comply with all applicable requirements.\n\n(e) All appointments shall expire in accordance with RSA 261:74-a, unless revoked pursuant to RSA 261:74-b or 74-f or these rules.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 519.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
